; Modular ERB: Addition/Add_Epitaph.ERB

@Add_Epitapth(FOR_DEATHMESSAGE = 0)
#DIM FOR_DEATHMESSAGE ;NAS custom
SIF !FOR_DEATHMESSAGE ;NAS custom
	PRINTFORML 당신은 %ARTICLE(SPLIT_G("big:old:odd-shaped:misshapen:broken:chipped:small:tiny:cross-shaped:tall:colored:black:marble:ancient:run-down:shiny:new:expensive-looking"))% 비석을 본다. 비문에는 다음과 같이 쓰여 있었다:
LOCALS = Not appreciating my puns while I was alive was a grave mistake.:Perhaps in his next incarnation he will have the wisdom to keep his sword sheathed.:Still fresh, still intact. Not before the inhabitants get hungry.:Never mind the broken bones - the cat had an accident on the way.:Nameless, faceless, kissless, loveless. You can do better than that.:The caskets are to remain sealed until further notice. We have a maniac on the loose.:Let it be known that the Mistress is kind enough to grant a swift death to all who is needy.:Ate too many peaches. Made for great fireworks, though.:He longed for love, but there were too many, and they never stopped.:Never stand between two furious women powerful enough to level mountains.:He broke her heart. She broke his spine.:Tea was particularly nasty that day.:He thought he had a Sake Bug. His pet Tsuchinoko ate well that day.:"I have told you not to trespass on my medicinal herb garden.":Who is the prettiest of them all? He answered wrong.:"I need to see if this liver thing actually works.":"I got here through death. Surely I can make it back the same way.":"What do you mean, I can't just grab some of these sunflowers and take them with me?":"Here's to a brave volunteer to test the new shiny jetpack. Didn't think it would explode, though. Rest in pieces.":Refused to water the flowers. They were very thirsty, too.:"This giant laser beam coming straight at me ain't shi-":"I hope one day to see my wife speak in the language I know.":"She said she'd make me immortal, I just had to die to see if the spell had done its magic.":Here lies a young exterminator, maybe it would have been better to listen to the Maiden.:Thoughts and prayers didn't calm the typhoon. May they comfort him in the hereafter.:"I was bored out of my mind, I challenged her before I could think right.":Therein the truth, lies. He knew too much.:He was too big, I was too small. My only regret is that I wasn't born a fairy.:"This looks like a good place for a picnic.":"I told you I wasn't good at holding back!":He said stop, but she never did...:Cross an oni - and you will find yourself lying beneath it.:"I thought this hypnosis thing was supposed to work!":"I think I'm fast enough to get back home without attracting anyone's attention.":"Excuse me, are these your panties?":Rest in peace... You were a mediocre plot device, at BEST.
SIF FLAG:周回数 && !FOR_DEATHMESSAGE
	LOCALS = %LOCALS%:Here lies %CALLNAME:MASTER% the %ORDINAL(FLAG:周回数)%.
LOCALS = %LOCALS%:%SPLIT_G("Her:His")% funeral was a grave affair.:%SPLIT_G("He:She")% always was known for her killer puns.:%SPLIT_G("He:She")% was dying to get into the funeral business.:What do you call a funeral ship? A sea hearse.:Speaking badly of the dead is a grave mistake.:Why do ghosts ride the cableway? To lift their spirits.:Did you hear the news about the graveyard? There are people dying to get in there.:Get well soon because headstones are expensive!:What's a corpse's favorite currency? Charisma.:What did the zombie say when she walked into the funeral home? Is your corpse tender here?:What's the difference between a corpse and a shirt? One's a casualty and the other is a casual tee.:Corpses aren't very funny—they're dead serious.:What are ghosts' favorite streets? Dead ends.:Even though your partner died, they'll always be your boo.:If you rush a decapitation, you'll get a head of yourself.:"At my funeral, I want a lot of flowers. It's on my bouquet list.":Auctioning a corpse? Now that's morbid!:It remains to be seen if it's an open casket.:He was dying to participate in a green funeral, he just didn't realize it would be his.:The story was about a funeral, but the plot had holes in it.:Planning %SPLIT_G("his:her")% funeral was a big undertaking.:Funeral prices have skyrocketed due to the cost of living.:"I thought the moon viewing was last night, but when I got there, the place was dead.":Dad always thought the last thing he needed was a burial plot. He was right.:Walking through the cemetery at night can put you in grave danger.:%SPLIT_G("He:She")% always had grave doubts about cemeteries.:"My music partner died while we were writing a new song. I guess she's now decomposing.":A will is a dead giveaway.:Never challenge shinigami to a pillow fight! Unless you are ready to handle the reaper cushions.:An artist was found dead in his home. The details are sketchy.:As an orchard grower, he enjoyed a fruitful life.:What does a liar do after he dies? He lies still!:"I made a grave mistake. But I was able to dig myself out of it.":Gravediggers often have trouble with coughin'.:I guess she finally urned her place in the family.:He used to ring the village bell, now he's a dead ringer.:Getting to see the other side takes spirit.:If you live each day as though it were your last, then one fated day it will be.:It was a grave error when the man was buried in the wrong plot.:Is it possible to be bored to death? That all depends on the drill.
LOCALS = %LOCALS%:The hole to Underworld opened before this bloke, just wished to die young. Desire smarter.:Here lies a man who died - Nobody mourned, nobody cried, how he lived, how he fared - Nobody knows, nobody cared.:Life is a jest, All things show it, I thought so once, Now I know it.:He wasn't afraid of death that came on his heels, No fear has here, and now he's there.:Fumbled a Spell Card, went out with a bang.:So much to do, so little done.:Came upon an evil witch, he didn't even think to run, and ended up in this ditch:His wife was constantly scolding and scoffing, so he sought for a repose in a 1200 yen coffin.:Had six swords, needed seven, now he's in heaven:"I came here to die, not to make a speech!":"I can see up your skirt.":"I told you I was sick!":A precious one from me has gone, I am left alone to carry on.:Sometimes, there is no poison like love.:Eat, drink and be merry, for tomorrow you may perish.:Grim death took %SPLIT_G("her")%, without any warning. Well at night, dead in the morning.:Here lies a master of knives, he could make quite a mess, killed while trying to put his babe in a dress:Love is your spirit in the sun, strength is your legacy you left, life is your essence never gone.:Learn the living from the dead, how easy breaks life's tender thread.:The old world is made brighter by the lives of folks like you.:We must all die, there's no doubt. Your glass is running... mine is out.:Here lies a man unmatched by all. "'e was such a givin' man, we will miss 'im with all our 'art" - Hot Spring attendant and the girls:The wild warrior was put to rest after a long life of great battles. May he rest in peace.:Here lies a non-believer, all dressed up, and no place to go.:Earth this casket keeps, and the sunbeams long to linger, where our sainted baby sleeps.:Beloved %SPLIT_G("mother:father:sister:brother:son:daughter")%.:Died before his time, he just wouldn't listen when we said "By Design".:Hit in the eye socket by a flying sky rocket.:Nothing is so sacred as honor, nothing is so loyal as love.:Many a heart by sorrow pressed, doth envy me my peaceful rest.:This spot is the sweetest I've seen in my life, for it raises my flowers and covers my wife.:"Hey! Who blew out the candle? Hello... Is anyone there?":Sleep with angels evermore.:Precious love, precious one, we will meet again, to be as one.:Weep not father and mother for me, for I am waiting in glory for thee.:Sleep on sweet baby, and take thy rest, God called thee home, She thought it best.:Step softly - a dream lies here.:Nary a drop, nary a one, dead anyway, because of a loon.:A rogue he was, such was his essence, but death he couldn't cheat, no matter how try. Be merciful to him and let him fly.:Was angry he like devil from the depths beneath, but not meaner than what killed him.:Do not grieve the Death, do not get up from the grave.:It is said he's fond of mixing, now he does not change the order of things:Wanted to be the hero, but choked on a fish bone.:Sometimes a spell is faster than flight.:Thought himself a soothsayer, never saw the blunt trauma coming.
LOCALS = %LOCALS%:Please don't dress in black\nWhen you're at my wake\nDon't go here to mourn\nBut to celebrate:Do not stand at my grave and weep. I am not there. I do not sleep. I am a thousand winds that blow. I am the diamond glints on snow.\nI am the sunlight on ripened grain. I am the gentle autumn rain. When you awaken in the morning's hush, I am the swift uplifting rush,\nOf quiet birds in circled flight. I am the soft stars that shine at night. Do not stand at my grave and cry\nI am not there. I did not die
;NAS Customs
IF FOR_DEATHMESSAGE
	RESULTS '= LOCALS
	RETURN
ENDIF
;==================
PRINTFORML 【%SPLIT_G(LOCALS)%】
